From 40799f5e892397a4ce81df0fb36357a25b7a607f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mali-re-kernel spike <spike@local>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 20:29:37 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 3/5] drm/lima: start the next task from the IRQ handler
 (upper-half scheduling)

The reference board's Android kernel builds the vendor Utgard r6p0 driver with
MALI_UPPER_HALF_SCHEDULING=1 (its __malidrv_build_info string): the PP
and GP interrupt handlers (mali_group_upper_half_pp ->
mali_executor_interrupt_pp 0xc039094c -> mali_executor_complete_group
0xc038f998 -> mali_executor_schedule) complete the job and start the next
queued one in the hard IRQ. Under the blob the Demo's dependent PP jobs
follow each other with no gap measurable from the capture (< 0.05 ms).

lima with drm_sched (credit_limit 1) needs a worker for that: the HW
fence callback queues free_job, whose work queues run_job, which flushes
the L2, switches the MMUs and starts the task, so every job-to-job step
pays a kworker wake-up plus free_job's BO puts.

Let drm_sched hand lima the next task while the current one runs
(credit_limit 2). run_job starts it at once if the pipe is idle, else
parks it in pipe->next_task, and lima_sched_pipe_task_done() starts it
from the IRQ handler before signalling the finished task. Only atomic-safe
work runs there: the GP heap-size fixup (it takes a BO mutex) moves to a
new task_prepare hook run from run_job, and a VM swapped out in the IRQ
is put later from free_job (or the start falls back to a work item).

Known gaps of this prototype: the timeout handler drops a queued task
and lets drm_sched resubmit it, but a task completing between its two
signalled checks and the IRQ mask is not handled specially.

Spike: RK3128 reference #375 (mali-re kernel area), not for upstream as is.
